# Revision Engine — working rules

An exam revision engine: administrators load past examination papers, students
sit them online as multiple-choice practice exams and are marked instantly.

## Hard constraints — do not break these

1. **Zero runtime dependencies.** `package.json` has an empty `dependencies`
   block and that is deliberate. Do NOT add Express, better-sqlite3, bcrypt,
   EJS, multer, dotenv, or any other package. Everything is built on Node's
   built-in modules. If a task seems to need a library, write it in
   `src/core/` or `src/lib/` instead, or say why the constraint should change —
   never quietly `npm install`.
2. **Node 22.5+ only.** The database is Node's built-in `node:sqlite`
   (`DatabaseSync`), not a native driver. `src/db.js` exits with a friendly
   message on older versions; keep that check.
3. **No build step.** No bundler, no transpiler, no TypeScript compile, no
   framework. Edit a file, restart (or `npm run dev`), reload the page.
4. **CommonJS**, not ESM. Use `require` / `module.exports`. Keep
   `"type": "commonjs"` in package.json.

## Layout

```
server.js            start-up, middleware pipeline, route registration, error pages
src/config.js        env config (.env loader written by hand)
src/db.js            SQLite connection + schema (node:sqlite)
src/seed.js          creates the first administrator and a sample exam
src/core/            the hand-rolled web framework
  app.js             router, middleware chain, req/res helpers
  body.js            urlencoded / JSON / multipart (file upload) parsing
  session.js         SQLite-backed sessions + CSRF tokens
  static.js          static file serving
  template.js        the HTML template engine
src/lib/password.js  scrypt hashing
src/lib/parsers/     question importers: text, csv, json, docx, pdf
src/middleware/auth.js  sign-in state, role guards, CSRF check, flash messages
src/models/          users, exams (+questions), attempts (+marking)
src/routes/          auth, student, admin handlers
views/               templates (.html)
public/              stylesheet + exam-runner script
sample-data/         example import files
```

## Template engine

`views/*.html` are compiled by `src/core/template.js`. The syntax is:

- `{{ expr }}` — HTML-escaped output (the default; use it for anything a user typed)
- `{{{ expr }}}` — raw output (only for trusted HTML, e.g. the layout's `body`)
- `{% if x %}` / `{% elif x %}` / `{% else %}` / `{% endif %}`
- `{% for item in list %}` / `{% for item, index in list %}` / `{% endfor %}`
- `{% set name = expr %}`
- `{% include "partials/foo.html" %}`
- `{# comment #}`

Expressions are plain JavaScript evaluated against the render data. **Every
variable a template references must exist in the render data** — the compiled
function uses `with(data)`, so a missing key throws a ReferenceError at render
time. When you add a variable to a template, add it to the `res.render(...)`
call too.

## Route handlers

Registered as `app.get(path, ...handlers)` / `app.post(...)` inside
`src/routes/*.js`, which each export a `register(app)` function called from
`server.js`. Path params use `:name` (`/admin/exams/:id/edit`).

Handlers receive `(req, res)` with:
`req.params`, `req.query`, `req.body`, `req.files`, `req.session`, `req.user`,
`res.render(view, data)`, `res.redirect(url)`, `res.json(data)`,
`res.send(body, contentType)`, `res.status(code)`.

Guards: `requireAdmin` for admin routes, `requireStudent` for signed-in pages.
Throw an error with `err.statusCode = 404` (or 403) to render the error page.

## Security rules — keep these intact

- Every POST form must include `<input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}">`.
  `verifyCsrf` rejects POSTs without a matching token. Fetch calls send it as
  the `X-CSRF-Token` header instead.
- All SQL uses prepared statements with bound parameters. Never build SQL by
  string concatenation.
- Passwords go through `src/lib/password.js` (scrypt). Never store or log a
  plain password.
- Output is escaped by `{{ }}`. Only use `{{{ }}}` for HTML you generated.
- Students may only read their own results; check ownership in the handler.

## Marking

In `src/models/attempts.js`. A question is correct only when the selected
option set matches the correct set **exactly** — so on a multiple-answer
question, one of two correct options scores zero, and both correct plus a wrong
one also scores zero. No negative marking. Marks default to 1 per question.

An attempt freezes its question order and option order at start time
(`question_ids` and `option_order` columns) so refreshing never reshuffles a
paper mid-exam. Preserve that behaviour.

## The exam runner

`views/student/attempt.html` renders **every** question into one form, and
`public/js/attempt.js` then shows one at a time with Previous/Next, the
numbered grid in the sidebar, and the left/right arrow keys. Two things follow
from that and must not be broken:

- Hiding a question does not stop its inputs being submitted, which is why the
  whole paper still posts in a single request. Never disable the inputs of a
  hidden question.
- Without JavaScript every question simply stays on the page and the form works
  as one long list. Keep that fallback: the pager starts with the `hidden`
  attribute and the script removes it.

Answers also save individually in the background (`POST /attempts/:id/answer`),
so a student can close the tab and resume where they left off — the runner
opens on the first unanswered question.

## Question importers

`src/lib/parsers/index.js` dispatches by file type. Each parser returns
`{ questions, issues }` — `issues` explains what could not be read so the
admin sees it on the import preview screen. Never silently drop a question:
add an entry to `issues`. The JSON parser also returns `exam`: settings read
from an optional `exam` block in the file, used by the create-an-exam-from-a-
file flow.

There are two import routes, both ending at a preview the admin must confirm:

- `/admin/import` — upload a file and it becomes a **new** exam. The preview
  shows an editable settings form, pre-filled from the file when it has an
  `exam` block.
- `/admin/exams/:id/import` — add questions to an exam that already exists.

Both render `views/admin/import.html` and `views/admin/import-preview.html`,
which branch on whether `exam` is set. The file picker must stay visible
without JavaScript — do not put it behind a tab or an accordion again.

Options are lettered A–J. The admin confirms on a preview screen before
anything is written to the database.

A question may carry a picture in `questions.image` — a `data:` URI, a
`/static/…` path or an `https://…` URL. Only the JSON and CSV importers can
supply one (`image` / `figure` / `diagram` columns or keys); the past-paper text
parser cannot, because plain text has nowhere to put a picture. The image
renders above the options in the exam runner and in the answer review. When a
paper's *options* are pictures, embed the whole lettered figure in the question
and make the option text "Shown at A", "Shown at B" and so on — and turn option
shuffling off for that exam, or the letters stop matching.

## Style

- Two-space indent, semicolons, single quotes in JS, double quotes in HTML attributes.
- `'use strict';` at the top of every JS file.
- British spelling in user-facing copy ("practise" as a verb, "organisation").
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*. Keep them sparse.
- Plain, direct copy in the UI. No exclamation marks.

## Running it

```bash
npm run seed      # create the database + first administrator
npm start         # http://localhost:3000
npm run dev       # auto-restart on file changes
npm run reset-db  # wipe everything and re-seed
```

There is no test runner in the repo. When you change marking, parsing or
auth, exercise the change by running the server and walking the flow.
